WEBVTT

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.830
Azuma-kun, I don't suppose...

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:12.440
you can tell me what this task 
only you can do is?

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:16.130
I'm sure there's some way I can help you.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:19.330
I was born and raised in 
this country, after all.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.680
No, after you've been so kind to me,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.760
I couldn't involve you in this, um...

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.510
Forgive me.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:32.810
For ridiculous grown-up reasons,
I can't readily give away my name.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:33.880
I see...

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.660
Still, I'm really happy that 
you've been so kind to me.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:46.690
Azuma-kun, pardon my asking, 
but where are your parents?

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:48.950
My dad died.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.690
I don't know where my mom is now,
or what she's doing.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.470
But I'm certain she's alive.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:01.870
Thank you very much.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:05.870
I pray you achieve your goal successfully.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.510
Okay. Thank you.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:30.150
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.150
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:45.160
BURANKI

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.830
BURANKI

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:52.630
BURANKI

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:12.520
Kazuki

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:12.520
Kaoruko

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.430
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:43.430
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.010
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.010
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:51.940
That's...

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:55.090
Justin's Buranki, Batolov.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:58.250
So he's here to take back Reoko-sama, huh?

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:02.170
That bastard Guy must have 
some serious interest in her.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.550
Anyway, where's Azuma?

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:07.340
I don't see him.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.260
Azuma's not here.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.290
What do you mean?

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.890
Azuma took off to save Kaoruko.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:16.750
So until he comes back, 
we'll fight without him.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.170
Fight?! Without a Buranki?!

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:20.800
Shut up! I'll kill you!

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.770
But still...

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.910
It'd be no fun if you showed 
yourselves so easily.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:37.610
They say the one qualified to 
wield Entei's heart is immortal.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:41.280
I'd love to find out if being 
crushed beneath this giant boulder

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.270
would put an end to that.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.080
Shuusaku, get Reoko-sama from upstairs.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.080
Got it.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.290
All right! Let's go, guys!

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.070
Yeah!

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:50.790
Right!

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.850
What's the matter, Shizuru-kun?

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:02.260
Uncle Akihito, you were those
two's teacher, weren't you?

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.530
You mean Lyudmila and Diana?

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:09.530
Yes. They were both excellent students.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.270
I wanted to hear them talk more.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:13.980
Hear them talk?

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.480
When they were fighting me,

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:20.780
they talked to their Bubuki a lot.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.020
It was a lot of fun to listen to.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:29.220
But now, neither of them 
will ever speak again.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.880
It's so very sad.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:34.790
Shizuru-kun...

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:43.220
It seems we both share a common goal now.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:49.080
In order to ensure no one else 
is sacrificed like they were,

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.270
we must defeat Guy.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:55.900
Shizuru-kun, let us fight 
together for what is right.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:59.520
That is what your shining power is for.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.380
Okay.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:29.350
You think you have a chance at defeating 
a Buranki with measly Bubuki?

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.740
I'll have to use a little trickery,

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.350
you fools!

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:42.940
Shizuru!

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.180
You cowards.

00:05:58.510 --> 00:05:59.860
What do we do, Hiiragi?

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:01.090
I'm thinking about it!

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:03.280
Damn it... What do we do?

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:04.400
What do we do?

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.360
Hey! You need to stay hidden!

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.590
They'll spot you!

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:13.600
Hiiragi-kun, do you want to 
defeat that Buranki, Batolov?

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:17.100
Obviously! Of course I want to win!

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:19.690
Do you feel that way from 
the bottom of your heart?

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:22.480
Yes. I'd give my life for it.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:26.110
You won't go back on that 
statement, will you?

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.110
That's right. I won't!

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:31.450
Good answer.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:35.940
That's exactly what best suits the 
user of Oubu's left foot, Iwatooshi.

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:51.010
Useless fools!

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:55.720
Then I will teach you all 
the true way to use Bubuki.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.220
The true way?

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:02.810
Yes. There's one thing Azuma-kun 
can do that you four can't.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.320
And what's that?

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:08.260
Hiiragi-kun, do you know 
where Iwatooshi's heart is?

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.280
Its heart?

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.650
Uh... When you come out 
and ask me where it is...

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:13.690
Where <i>is</i> it?

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:15.200
I know!

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.070
It's here.

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:20.750
Shizuru-kun, well done.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:25.890
Yes, this is where you can find 
their heart, their nucleus.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.740
When Azuma-kun controls Oubu,

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:33.930
his own heart is superimposed 
on the Bubuki's nucleus.

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:36.040
I get it.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.260
So that's how he's able to 
pull forth Oubu's true power.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:42.940
What Azuma's been doing that we haven't...

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:47.690
You mean we have to merge our own 
hearts with our Bubuki's nucleus?

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:51.700
That's right. Well done.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:56.200
Th-Then you should've told 
us so to begin with!

00:07:56.550 --> 00:08:01.460
I reached that solution on my 
own when I was around your age.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:04.320
You kids were poorer 
students than I expected,

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:06.950
so I had no choice but to tell you.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:12.720
Now...

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:15.960
It's time to put that into practice!

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.190
Hey, Epizo.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:31.900
I'm tired. Let's go back to Demokratia.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:35.860
If you apologize, I'm sure 
Monsieur Guy will forgive you.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.620
Besides, Mega-lala's unique 
waveform is probably

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.870
giving away our location, anyway.

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:48.130
Epizo, is something wrong?

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:52.400
Farrah, I think I'm sick.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:54.620
Huh? What do you mean?

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:59.350
Well, like, my chest feels all 
hot or hazy or something.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.890
Epizo, what did you pick 
up off the ground and eat?

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.160
I've only eaten the same 
stuff you guys have!

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:09.110
I've had nothing but french fries!

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.780
Also, where would I even pick up any food?!

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:16.530
So when are your symptoms the worst?

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.720
Uh, well...

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.530
When I'm thinking about things.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.000
Thinking? You?!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.450
Yeah, when I think about Laetitia,

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:28.880
my chest starts to feel all tight.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.590
Then suddenly, I'm like,

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:33.010
"Augh!" And then...

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.590
Epizo... That's...

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:37.980
You know what it is, Farrah?!

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:39.720
Am I sick?! Is it a sickness?!

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:42.470
That's...

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:46.100
Heartburn! You ate too many french fries!

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.690
Epizo, you glutton!

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:51.560
Heartburn? Oh! Burning breast!

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.010
I see! So that's what it was!

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.860
Great! Thank goodness!

00:09:56.690 --> 00:09:58.880
Gosh, we were worried over nothing.

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:02.230
We're having you go out to buy 
the food next time, Epizo.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.490
Burning breast! Yeah!

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.320
Ow...

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:34.570
Azuma? What are you doing here?!

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:37.230
That's what I want to ask you!

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:39.070
What?!

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:40.290
What?!

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:43.080
Found them!

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:43.880
This way!

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:48.520
I'm sure you two have a lot to talk 
about, but save it for later!

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:49.540
Zetsubi's here, too?

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:53.230
That's Zetsubi-<i>san</i>!
Don't forget the "san," Azuma!

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:55.250
G-Got it, Zetsubi-san.

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:00.760
The Buranki Epimew!

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.300
Laetitia!

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:05.850
I cannot allow you to escape!

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:12.020
Okay, I'm counting on you, Iwatooshi.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.290
What is that light?

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:38.510
Hmph. Incorrigible.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.350
Wh-What is this?!

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.270
Understand, Hiiragi-kun?

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:53.700
That form is specialized for attacking.

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:56.360
Don't forget that it carries risks,

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:59.740
since there's no barrier to protect you.

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:04.990
I didn't teach you this just 
so you could run off and die.

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:07.050
This can't be...

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:10.490
This is incredible!

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:16.000
<b>Episode 19
Older Brother
 and Younger Sister</b>

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:16.000
<b><i>BUBUKI BURANKI
The Gentle Giants
 of the Galaxy</i></b>

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.550
<b><i>BUBUKI BURANKI</i></b>

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:20.550
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:28.020
Zetsubi-san!

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:30.600
Don't worry about me! You two go ahead!

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:39.690
I can get out on my own! Stay out of my way!

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:42.360
We have a better chance 
if we escape together!

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.320
Stop trying to act like a big brother!

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:46.990
I'm not acting! I am your big brother!

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:52.120
Why are you always like that?

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:55.160
No matter what's going on,
you act all cool and composed.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.830
I look like an idiot for being so on edge!

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:03.220
The way you act like you're totally 
fine when you're really not...

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:06.540
That's why I always get the 
short end of the stick!

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:08.200
I always lose!

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:09.760
Kaoruko...

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:12.220
Why were you born at the same time as me?!

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:16.440
You were the only one our parents praised 
and cared about! It's not fair!

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:20.610
I'm smarter, my grades are better,
and I have more brains!

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:24.110
Why are you always the one 
treated as more valuable?!

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:26.620
That's not true.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:28.780
You're the one treated as more valuable.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:32.290
Then tell me why I've been 
alone all this time!

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:39.340
Dad said to give this to you.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:52.830
Ouch...

00:13:56.570 --> 00:13:57.890
Are you okay?

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:00.530
No problem.

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:04.500
The air still tastes so sweet here.

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:08.590
Thank you, Duroc.

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:11.150
It was no trouble.

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:14.500
But I cannot stay long.

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:17.230
Yes, I know.

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:19.500
Thank you so much.

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:22.500
Welcome home.

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.010
Thanks!

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:31.010
Don't you think you're overdoing it?

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:34.010
It's hard on you, isn't it?

00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:39.290
Just coming up here took a 
serious toll on your health.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:41.220
You've really pushed yourself too far.

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:44.020
Can you tell that from my Rinzu or whatever?

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:45.360
Well, yes.

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:50.200
That stuff is completely over my head.

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:53.660
That's the great thing about you, Akira-san.

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:58.510
What about you?

00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:00.500
Are you doing all right?

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.400
It seems strange, even to me,

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:06.020
but as you can see, I'm quite well.

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:07.940
It really is strange.

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:09.400
I see.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.060
That's good, then.

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:24.020
It was from here...

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:25.310
Huh?

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:31.430
I was always watching you,
Azuma, and Kaoruko.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.590
All this time.

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:35.720
I see.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:38.780
Crap, that's right!

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:40.910
I came to get something I forgot!

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:42.630
Something you forgot?

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:43.960
Yeah.

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:47.200
Something really important.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:58.430
Azuma...

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:02.940
Your father asked me to give you this.
It's his wish for you.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:04.760
Here.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:08.710
He said to give it to you myself.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.450
I don't need that stupid toy!

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:26.510
This belongs to you.

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:30.420
Kaoruko, listen to me.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.010
Dad died on Treasure Island.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.390
Don't lie to me! That can't be true!

00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:51.030
I'll never believe that.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:52.900
I'll never allow that!

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.830
He left me alone all this time,

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:58.620
and then he goes and dies?

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.080
What is that?

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.790
Was my life just one big Hell?

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.290
Dad didn't want to get you

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:11.620
involved in the battle 
over Bubuki and Buranki.

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:17.450
He said that it was my job 
as your older brother,

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:19.480
as a man, to protect you.

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:23.790
That's why he took me around 
the world with him.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:27.770
He wanted to make me the 
strongest man in the world.

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:40.780
What?

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:42.750
What are you doing?

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.580
I got stronger, too!

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:49.710
I got strong enough to protect myself!

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.720
<b>Kaoruko</b>

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:22.170
Talking about how it's a man's job...

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:27.320
Dad's way of thinking is so outdated.

00:18:27.860 --> 00:18:28.710
Kaoruko...

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:31.640
I'm sorry we left you alone.

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:34.150
I really am sorry.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:42.660
Kaoruko...

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.100
I was so lonely.

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:50.290
Onii-chan!

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:19.430
I've been told that I may eliminate 
you two if you resist.

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:22.220
Prepare yourselves.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:30.520
That's...

00:19:31.070 --> 00:19:33.020
The Buranki Zampaza?

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:35.020
Who's piloting it?

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:41.200
Yo! Long time no see, Azuma!

00:19:42.350 --> 00:19:43.440
Arabashiri?

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:44.730
What's this?

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:48.080
Would that be the little 
sister I've heard about?

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:49.990
What a cutie!

00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:56.660
Well, there's a lot I'd like to say,

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:58.960
but first we've gotta get out of here!

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:06.570
Damn... I might've managed 
to fool it with this,

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:09.830
but I never had what it took to work 
this thing in the first place!

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:16.770
Use that, Kaoruko!

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:17.540
Huh?

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:21.970
That's the heart linked to Zampaza's body!

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:25.450
I stole one that was adjusted 
so you could use it!

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:28.450
Kaoruko, use that to fight for now!

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:31.390
I can't operate Zampaza to its fullest!

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:32.710
You have to!

00:20:35.970 --> 00:20:37.530
I guess I have no choice!

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:40.860
When a grown man is bowing his 
head and crying for my help,

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:42.590
I just can't refuse.

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:45.390
What?! You're way too full of yourself!

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:49.010
Zampaza!

00:20:55.900 --> 00:21:00.520
Sheesh! That sister of yours is 
one unbelievable little girl.

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:01.770
You think so?

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:05.520
Souya, how is she operating a 
Buranki with intact limbs when

00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:07.070
she only has its heart?

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:11.370
That bastard Guy established 
the technology himself,

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:14.250
using Maxim and his team as his lab rats.

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:16.440
So that's it.

00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:19.530
Thank you for your help all this time.

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:22.810
Go on back to your partner.

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:40.400
You're still going to keep fighting 
in that condition, Laetitia?

00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:42.680
I won't go easy on you.

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:50.880
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:53.420
The greatest heart user of the century,

00:21:53.420 --> 00:21:56.790
the girl of unrivaled beauty, Kazuki Kaoruko,

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:58.360
is about to show you a turning of the

00:21:58.360 --> 00:22:00.900
tables that will make blood 
boil and flesh dance,

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:04.300
right here in France, in the biggest 
panic sale you've ever seen!

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:06.050
If you blink,

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:08.810
you'll miss it!
